@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix xml: <http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@base <https://ontoboard.org/patterns/mwo-temporal-region.owl> .

<https://ontoboard.org/patterns/mwo-temporal-region.owl> rdf:type owl:Ontology .

# MWO 3.0.2 reading of Pattern 7 "Temporal region" (https://ise-fizkarlsruhe.github.io/mwo/docs/patterns/).
# The figure was drawn against MWO 3.0.0. Every term below was checked against the 3.0.2 release; domains, ranges and
# characteristics are 3.0.2's own and none is narrowed to the classes the figure draws.
# Edges of the figure (tail --property--> head); all nine are carried:
#   process --occupies temporal region--> 1-D temporal region     obo:BFO_0000199 (functional: ONE region per process)
#   1-D temporal region --has proper temporal part--> 1-D temporal region
#                                                            obo:BFO_0000181; the figure's label 'proper_temporal_part' has no has/of,
#                                                            the arrow reads 'has' (the inverse is obo:BFO_0000136, declared too)
#   1-D temporal region --has first instant--> temporal instant   obo:BFO_0000222 (the figure says 'has_first_instance')
#   1-D temporal region --has last instant--> temporal instant    obo:BFO_0000224 (the figure says 'has_last_instance')
#   1-D temporal region --denoted by--> specification datum       obo:IAO_0000235; pmdco:PMD_0060009
#   0-D temporal region --denoted by--> specification datum
#   process --denoted by--> event frequency datum                 mwo:MWO_0001001
#   specification datum --has value--> literal                    nfdi:NFDI_0001007
#   event frequency datum --has value--> literal
# The figure draws the two instants as zero-dimensional temporal regions; MWO ranges has first / last instant over temporal
# instant (obo:BFO_0000203, a subclass of the zero-dimensional region), so that is the class the instants have here.
# The figure also draws the process occupying TWO regions. occupies temporal region is functional, so a process has one;
# the worked example gives it one and relates the second by has proper temporal part.

